If a period of length $m$ contains $r$ free levels, then $k$ complete periods contain $rk$ free levels. Each free level doubles the viable count, so $N(mk)=2^{rk}$ and $d_{mk}=rk/(mk)=r/m$. An incomplete final period contributes only a bounded error, proving convergence to $r/m$.
</details>

## Realizing any rational geometry

Every rational $p/q$ in $[0,1]$ is obtained by taking $p$ free positions in a period of length $q$.

